//! Round-102 regression pins for the TMOP metric zoo.
//!
//! Every row pins values produced by the MFEM 4.10 C++ oracle
//! (`tmp/d102tmop/d102_dump_metric.cpp`, built against mfem410_ser) on the
//! deterministic synthetic Jacobians generated by [`sample_jpt`] below — the
//! same generator the C++ oracle uses, so the pins reproduce exactly.
//!
//! Per id: (id, EvalW of synthetic record 0, EvalW of record 1, EvalP[0] of
//! record 0, AssembleH[0] of record 0). Records 0/1 use W = I and W =
//! R(0.7)·diag(1.3, 0.9) (2D) / R(0.4)·R(0.9)·diag(1.2, 0.8, 1.1) (3D)
//! respectively, exercising the target-dependent A-metrics.
//!
//! Metrics 211/313 have no C++ derivative path (MFEM aborts in EvalP/
//! AssembleH); their EP/EH pins are empty and the fem-rs analytic derivatives
//! are instead verified against finite differences of their own EvalW /
//! EvalP in [`d102_no_cpp_deriv_metrics_are_fd_consistent`].
//!
//! Driver parameter conventions (mesh-optimizer / tmop-check-metric):
//! gamma = 0.5 (66/80/332/333/334/347) / 0.9 (49/126), eps = 1e-4 (211/311),
//! tauval = min_det = -0.1 (22/252/313/352).

